531:## Rules & Hooks
533:16 rules + 7 hooks. The rules are tiered contracts: of the 13 plugin-managed rule files, `discretion.md` resolves every instruction in the other 12 to exactly one of Anchor / Default / Guidance, and the 3 user-owned override files resolve Anchor-first under their parent rules. Nine plugin rules load at launch and four when a matching file is read; the detailed procedures live in contracts read on demand ([Why v5](#why-v5), [docs/rules.md](docs/rules.md)). The hook set is 4 advisory reminder hooks plus an auto-formatter and two blocking guards. The reminder roles differ per hook: the Stop and post-compact hooks render owed-gate reminders from the digest-bound state (`review-state.js`), the prompt hook prints the `[AUTO_LOOP_STATE]` fact line, the post-skill hook prints a static gate-order line, and the post-compact hook also re-injects the git baseline; the review layer never blocks — pre-edit-guard still blocks sensitive-path edits (a security guard; it needs `jq` and does not fire without it), pre-bash-codex-launch-guard blocks a Codex dispatch launched with its progress redirected away from the task panel, and the hard gates live at the git level (commit-msg-guard, installed by `/codex-setup init`; pre-push-gate, opt-in).
535:**What the plugin runs and reaches.** Review skills shell out to the [Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex), which sends each review prompt, and the repository files Codex reads in its read-only sandbox, to OpenAI under your own Codex configuration. Git and CI skills call `gh`, which reaches GitHub for pull requests, CI runs and the `gh stack` extension; a push runs only after your per-use approval. `/deep-research` and other research skills fetch web pages. Hooks run the plugin's own shell and Node scripts locally, and the post-edit formatter runs `prettier` only when the project has it in `node_modules/.bin`, or has a Prettier config file and a `prettier` on `PATH` — no hook downloads anything.
537:**Usage-limit wrap-up.** When a Claude subscription reaches its usage limit mid-task, recent Claude Code versions can give Claude a small allowance to reach a stopping point. That helps a change end in a clean state; it does not close a gate. A review or `/precommit` still owed stays owed, and the Stop hook's reminder may not appear during the allowance, so read `review-state.js check` or the next `[AUTO_LOOP_STATE]` line before treating the work as done. This is host behaviour, documented here and not tested by this repository.
539:> **Customization**: Edit `auto-loop-project.md` to override auto-loop behavior per project. Plugin updates won't conflict — see [Rule Override Pattern](docs/features/rule-override-pattern/2-tech-spec.md).
541:For full rules, hooks, and environment variable reference, see [docs/rules.md](docs/rules.md) and [docs/hooks.md](docs/hooks.md).
